# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, git stores whatever bytes the working tree happens to
# contain. A file rewritten by a different editor then shows as every line
# changed, which buries real edits: on 16 Aug 2026 `git status` listed 24
# modified files, of which 15 had actually changed and 9 differed only by
# carriage returns.
#
# text=auto stores every text file with LF in the repository and checks it out
# with the platform's own endings, so Windows editors keep working and the
# history stays clean.
* text=auto

# Never transformed. Rewriting line endings inside these corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.pyc binary
